  "flags": {
    "mgt2": {
      "demo": {
        "order": 36,
        "cliff": "an education is a career Item that runs a different set of rolls",
        "teaches": [
          "kind: preCareer turns the same career Item into an education: the loop runs its entry, its skills, one Pre-career Event and a graduation, and no Survival, commission or Benefit roll.",
          "preCareer.tied names the career the school feeds, and a pick with tied: true reads that career's own table, so editing the patrol edits what its school teaches.",
          "Graduation has three arms: pass, honours applied on top of the pass, and fail, which runs only above failFloor; at the floor or below nothing is left.",
          "A tray entry scoped firstAfterGraduation is bound to the first career entered after the school, or dropped if that first attempt is refused."
        ],
        "trap": "kind: preCareer leaves the career half of the type inert: rankLadders, assignments, tables, benefits and mishapTable stay empty because nothing reads them. perPreviousCareer is 0 because a printed education entry carries only its termDMs, and years is blank so the term lasts the kind's four. The eleven record fields below the tables stay empty, as on every template."
      }
    }
  },
